#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""citygen — Phase 3.13: write the city data files (screenplays/tasks/cities/<planet>_<city>.lua) for the stock cities.

Facts come from the stock data (city regions, mission cities, travel points, the stock city screenplays' walking loops,
the world snapshot through tools/lotsurvey) and from the running server through the lab oracles (landAt: terrain,
water, no-build; pathBetween: the navmesh). Every generated point is written into the city file as a plain number
with a comment saying where it came from, so the shipped data is explicit and reviewable.

  tools/citygen plan                       the cities this tool knows and what each gets
  tools/citygen write [KEY…] [--dry]       write the city files (all planned cities, or the keys given)
  tools/citygen spots PLANET X Y [R]       print land points around a centre (weather parties, story camps)

Server probes go through `tools/swg cmd --shared` (read-only oracles, no bench lock) and are cached in
~/.swg-lab/citygen/ — terrain never changes. Needs the server up with a lab that has landAt/pathBetween.
"""
